          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>Which of the following is a characteristic advantage of live attenuated vaccines</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which of the following is a characteristic advantage of live attenuated vaccines over inactivated vaccines?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>They do not require cold chain maintenance</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Live attenuated vaccines are often more temperature-sensitive and require strict cold chain — some (e.g., OPV, varicella) need freezer storage at −20°C.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>They contain purified antigenic subunits with minimal reactogenicity</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Purified subunit antigens characterise inactivated or subunit vaccines, not live attenuated ones — live vaccines contain whole weakened organisms.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>They produce the strongest and most long-lasting immunity, often after only 1–2 doses</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Because they closely mimic natural infection, live attenuated vaccines activate both humoral and cell-mediated immunity, producing robust and durable protection.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>They can be safely administered to all immunocompromised patients</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Live attenuated vaccines carry the risk of vaccine-strain disease in immunocompromised individuals and are generally contraindicated in this group.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Live attenuated vaccines are weakened through serial passage to abolish pathogenicity while retaining immunogenicity. They mimic natural infection more closely than any other vaccine type, producing the strongest, most durable immunity — often requiring only 1–2 doses."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! Live attenuated vaccines (e.g., BCG, OPV, MMR, varicella, yellow fever) mimic natural infection closely, stimulating both arms of immunity — this is why they confer the strongest and most long-lasting protection."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
                "enableSolutionsButton": true,
                "enableCheckButton": true,
